</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Resolution-Aware Test-Time Calibration</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While recent methods have extended diffusion models to arbitrary resolutions by adapting token lengths or position encodings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, we focus instead on correcting forward-reverse misalignment through test-time adjustment of the conditioning noise level. Rather than modifying the sampling trajectory or retraining the model, we propose a lightweight post-processing procedure that adjusts only the input noise level <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> passed to the denoiser at each timestep.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Role of Noise-Level Embedding.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each timestep, diffusion models receive not only the noisy latent <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> but also a noise-level or timestep embedding that encodes the expected magnitude of corruption in the input. This embedding allows the model to adapt its prediction of the denoised image based on how noisy the input is: for low noise, the model performs minor corrections, whereas for high noise, it applies stronger denoising. In our framework, the conditioning noise <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is directly mapped to this embedding. Consequently, by manipulating <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at test time, we can explicitly interfere how the model interprets the noise level in the input, enabling a resolution-aware correction without changing the learned weights or the sampling schedule.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Problem Setup.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> denote a trained flow-matching diffusion model with a predefined noise schedule <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sigma_{t}}{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sigma_{t}}{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. At each timestep <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the model receives a noisy latent <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and a noise-level embedding derived from a conditioning noise <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. This embedding informs the network how much noise to expect and guides its prediction of the velocity field <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\mathbf{x}_{t+1},\hat{\sigma}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\mathbf{x}_{t+1},\hat{\sigma}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In standard sampling, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}=\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}=\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> follows the original noise schedule. In our approach, we allow <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to differ from <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to correct forward–reverse misalignment at test time. By tuning <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can adapt the model’s denoising behavior to different resolutions without changing the learned weights or sampling procedure.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Given a noisy latent input <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we expect <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to match the forward sample obtained by applying Gaussian noise to a clean latent <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to find a conditioning noise level <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the denoised prediction <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes the discrepancy from <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{t+1}+\phi(\mathbf{x}_{t+1},\hat{\sigma}_{t})\cdot\Delta t,\quad\text{where }\Delta t=\sigma_{t+1}-\sigma_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{t+1}+\phi(\mathbf{x}_{t+1},\hat{\sigma}_{t})\cdot\Delta t,\quad\text{where }\Delta t=\sigma_{t+1}-\sigma_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}=\arg\min_{\hat{\sigma}}\;\|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}-\mathbf{x}_{t}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}=\arg\min_{\hat{\sigma}}\;\|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}-\mathbf{x}_{t}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coarse-to-Fine Search Strategy.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We estimate <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> via a coarse-to-fine grid search that minimizes the one-step reverse error at each timestep. Starting from the final step <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T{-}1</annotation></semantics></math>, we proceed backward in time. For each <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we first evaluate the default conditioning <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}=\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}=\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, then perform a coarse sweep with a larger stride <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to identify a promising region. A subsequent fine-grained search with a smaller stride <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> refines the estimate within a narrow window.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure monotonic consistency with the diffusion trajectory, we constrain all candidate values to lie in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\hat{\sigma}_{t+1}^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\hat{\sigma}_{t+1}^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math>. This backward recursion allows us to progressively calibrate the denoising inputs while respecting the ordering of noise levels. The full procedure is detailed in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Resolution-Dependent Misalignment. ‣ 3.2 Train-Test Misalignment in Diffusion Sampling ‣ 3 Method ‣ NoiseShift: Resolution-Aware Noise Recalibration for BetterLow-Resolution Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We perform this calibration over a small set of
image-text pairs for each resolution. The resulting schedule <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is resolution-specific and cached for reuse at inference.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference with Calibrated Conditioning.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At inference time, we sample using the original noise schedule <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to preserve the intended diffusion trajectory. However, at each timestep <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we replace the model input conditioning with the precomputed value <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained from the calibration procedure. These values are resolution-specific but fixed across inputs, and require no model retraining or architectural changes. As shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Inference with Calibrated Conditioning. ‣ 3.3 Resolution-Aware Test-Time Calibration ‣ 3 Method ‣ NoiseShift: Resolution-Aware Noise Recalibration for BetterLow-Resolution Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the update step becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{t+1}+\phi(\mathbf{x}_{t+1},\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*})\cdot(\sigma_{t+1}-\sigma_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{t+1}+\phi(\mathbf{x}_{t+1},\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*})\cdot(\sigma_{t+1}-\sigma_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Euler Sampling with Calibrated Conditioning</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
                
                
               Model <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, initial latent <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, noise schedule <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, calibrated conditioning <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}\}_{t=0}^{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*}\}_{t=0}^{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T-1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{t}\leftarrow\phi(\mathbf{x}_{t+1},\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{t}\leftarrow\phi(\mathbf{x}_{t+1},\hat{\sigma}_{t}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{t+1}+\mathbf{v}_{t}\cdot(\sigma_{t+1}-\sigma_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{t+1}+\mathbf{v}_{t}\cdot(\sigma_{t+1}-\sigma_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
